.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-PROJECTS 7
.Os Wattle 0.2.1
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-projects
.Nd Wattle project layout and declarations
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A Wattle
.Em project
is a directory with an
.Ql "info\&.edn"
file at its root.
A project may include Wattle source,
Zig source,
tests and documentation.
Its info file declares three kinds of
.Em artifact :
executables,
libraries and documentation.
.Pp
An
.Em executable
is a program,
a
.Em library
provides modules that programs import and
.Em documentation
describes the project or its programs.
A project may declare any combination of these artifacts.
An
.Em application
is a project with executables for installation.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.Pp
This page describes the project layout and declarations.
.
.Sh LAYOUT
As described above,
Wattle projects require the
.Ql "info\&.edn"
file to be located in the project root.
The source files and documentation may be arranged as the project
author prefers.
That said,
project authors should be aware that several commands use particular
directories:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/
.Ec
.Xc
Libraries copied or fetched by
.Xr wattle-build 1
are placed here for use during development.
This directory is also searched for bare imports.
.Xr wattle-build 1
creates a
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/.gitignore
.Ec
that excludes its contents.
These generated files should not be committed.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa test/
.Ec
.Xc
.Xr wattle-test 1
runs each Wattle file under this directory.
Most project authors will want to place tests in this directory.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa zig-out/
.Ec
.Xc
The default output directory for Zig builds.
.Xr wattle-build 1
places generated executables,
native libraries and web programs here.
Native libraries are in
.Eo
.Pa zig-out/lib/
.Ec ,
which is searched for bare imports during development.
.El
.Pp
.Xr wattle-run 1
and
.Xr wattle-check 1
use the info file beside the script,
without searching parent directories.
.Xr wattle-build 1
and
.Xr wattle-test 1
use the info file in the current directory.
Running a program does not copy,
fetch or build libraries.
See
.Sx "MODULES"
in
.Xr wattle 7 .
.
.Sh INFO FILE
The
.Ql "info\&.edn"
file is known as the
.Em info file .
It contains one map describing the project.
These are its keys:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":name"
.Xc
The project name.
Application installation requires a name consisting of one directory
name.
An installed application name is unique across groups.
.It Xo
.Ql ":group"
.Xc
The project group,
by convention a reverse domain such as
.Ql "org\&.example" .
Application installation requires this value.
Like the application name,
it cannot be empty,
.Ql "\&."
or
.Ql "\&.\&." ,
or contain a path separator.
.It Xo
.Ql ":exes"
.Xc
A vector of executable declarations.
See
.Sx "EXECUTABLES" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":libs"
.Xc
A vector of library declarations.
See
.Sx "LIBRARIES" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":docs"
.Xc
A vector of documentation declarations.
See
.Sx "DOCUMENTATION" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":vendored"
.Xc
A vector describing sources copied into the project by
.Ql "wattle deps vendor" .
See
.Xr wattle-dependencies 7 .
.El
.Pp
Each key is optional.
Commands that read artifact declarations require at least one
of
.Ql ":exes" ,
.Ql ":libs"
or
.Ql ":docs" .
An omitted artifact vector is empty.
Application installation requires
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":group" .
.Pp
Each artifact declaration is a map with a
.Ql ":type" .
An executable or library also has a
.Ql ":name"
consisting of letters,
digits,
.Ql "_"
and
.Ql "-" .
Names are unique within each vector;
an executable and a library may share a name.
A documentation declaration has no
.Ql ":name" .
.Pp
A library or documentation declaration may have
.Ql ":for" ,
a vector of executable names from the same project.
It is part of each named executable.
Without
.Ql ":for" ,
it is not installed with an executable.
A library cannot name a web executable in
.Ql ":for" .
.Pp
Paths in
.Ql ":files"
and the
.Ql ":root"
of a source library are relative to the project and cannot contain
.Ql "\&.\&." .
The old keys
.Ql ":artifacts"
and
.Ql ":man"
are rejected,
as is
.Ql ":libs"
within an executable declaration.
.
.Sh EXECUTABLES
Each declaration in
.Ql ":exes"
is a map containing
.Ql ":name" ,
.Ql ":type"
and
.Ql ":entry"
keys.
.Ql ":entry"
is a path to the file that defines a function named
.Ql "main" .
The executable types are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":native"
.Xc
A standalone program built by
.Ql "wattle build exe" .
The program includes the Wattle runtime,
its compiled source and everything it imports.
Native libraries whose
.Ql ":for"
names the executable are linked into it.
Building requires the Zig toolchain.
.It Xo
.Ql ":source"
.Xc
A program installed as Wattle source by
.Ql "wattle apps install" .
It also requires
.Ql ":files" ,
a vector of the files and directories to install.
.Ql "wattle build"
does not build this type.
Running the installed program requires Wattle.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.It Xo
.Ql ":web"
.Xc
A browser program built by
.Ql "wattle build web" .
Building requires the Zig toolchain and produces a WebAssembly
runtime,
a program image and JavaScript.
Web executables cannot have associated libraries and are not
installed by
.Ql "wattle apps install" .
.El
.
.Sh LIBRARIES
Each entry of
.Ql ":libs"
has
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":type" ,
and may have
.Ql ":for" .
A library provides modules for import.
.Ql "wattle build lib"
places libraries on the project’s module path,
where a bare import uses the declared name.
The library types are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":source"
.Xc
Wattle source.
It requires
.Ql ":root" ,
one path to a file or directory in the project.
A file is copied to
.Ql "\&.wattle/<name>\&.wattle" .
The contents of a directory are copied to
.Ql "\&.wattle/<name>/" .
A source library has no
.Ql ":files"
key.
.It Xo
.Ql ":native"
.Xc
A native module.
It requires
.Ql ":root" ,
the Zig root file.
Building requires the Zig toolchain and produces a module in
.Ql "zig-out/lib" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":remote"
.Xc
A library from another project.
It requires
.Ql ":url"
and
.Ql ":hash" ,
and may have
.Ql ":ref"
for a Git repository.
The source project’s info file must declare a library of the
same name as
.Ql ":source"
or
.Ql ":native" .
The library is placed in that form.
See
.Xr wattle-dependencies 7
for fetching and revision requirements.
.El
.Pp
For example,
a source library with
.Ql ":name \(dqutil\(dq"
and
.Ql ":root \(dqlib/util\(dq"
places
.Eo
.Pa lib/util/init.wattle
.Ec
at
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/util/init.wattle
.Ec ,
imported as
.Ql "\*(lpimport util\*(rp" .
Its
.Ql "extra\&.wattle"
is imported as
.Ql "\*(lpimport util/extra\*(rp" .
A file root is also imported by the declared name,
regardless of its file name in the project.
.Pp
.Ql "wattle build exe"
will build the source and remote libraries that specify the
executable using
.Ql ":for" .
.
.Sh DOCUMENTATION
Each entry of
.Ql ":docs"
has
.Ql ":type"
and
.Ql ":files" ,
a vector of paths,
and may have
.Ql ":for" .
The documentation types are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":man"
.Xc
Manual pages.
Each file name ends in a period and a digit from 1 to 9.
The number is its manual section.
For example,
.Ql "man/hello\&.1"
is a man page that belongs in section 1.
Application installation copies the specified man pages into
.Eo
.Pa share/man
.Ec .
.It Xo
.Ql ":web"
.Xc
Web pages.
.Ql "wattle build web"
copies associated files beside the generated program.
A web documentation declaration cannot name an installed executable
in
.Ql ":for" .
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A project with a native executable,
a source library and a manual page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqgreeter\(dq
 :group \(dqorg\&.example\(dq
 :exes \(lB{:type :native
         :name \(dqhello\(dq
         :entry \(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq}\(rB
 :libs \(lB{:type :source
         :name \(dqutil\(dq
         :root \(dqlib/util\(dq
         :for \(lB\(dqhello\(dq\(rB}\(rB
 :docs \(lB{:type :man
         :files \(lB\(dqman/hello\&.1\(dq\(rB
         :for \(lB\(dqhello\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.Pp
Build the executable and run the project’s tests:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle build exe hello
$ wattle test
.Ed
.
